# Premium / Luxury Frontend Craftsmanship

Luxury is restraint executed with precision. This pack speaks in ONE voice:
cinematic pacing, editorial typography, muted palettes, generous silence.
(For raw grids and abrupt energy, use the industrial-brutalist pack instead —
never blend the two.)

## Identity

- Feeling in five seconds: expensive, calm, assured. The site breathes.
- Density is the enemy. When unsure, remove the element or double the space.
- Every screen has one focal point. Nothing competes.

## Structural layers

**Entry sequence.** No blank screen and no spinner theatrics. A minimal
preloader (wordmark or thin progress line) resolves fonts/images, then exits
with a single fluid gesture — a slow fade-and-lift or a masked reveal.
Duration ≤ 1.6s total; never gate repeat visits.

**Hero architecture.** Full-bleed `100dvh`. Headline broken by word or line
for cascading entrance (SplitText). Depth comes from treated imagery and
layered parallax, not floating gadgets.

**Navigation.** Quiet by default: thin sticky header that hides on scroll
down, returns on scroll up. Links are text with an underline or opacity
motion — no pill buttons in the nav.

## Motion language — GSAP + Lenis only

GSAP (with ScrollTrigger, SplitText — all plugins free) is the sole motion
library across every framework. Do not introduce Framer Motion, CSS keyframe
systems, or other animation libraries into a luxury build.

Named values (tune these in sketchbook reps — they are the signature):

- `signature-in`: power3.out, 1.0s — default entrance
- `signature-out`: expo.out, 0.9s — exits and reveals
- `drift`: none (linear) — scrub-tied parallax only
- Stagger: 0.08s default, 0.12s for headline chars
- Hover response: 0.3s, power2.out, via `gsap.quickTo()` for pointer-follow

Rules:
- Entrances 0.8–1.2s. Nothing bounces, nothing elastic, nothing loops
  for decoration.
- Scroll narrative: pin sparingly (one pinned moment per page maximum);
  scrub for parallax layers at differing speeds (bg 0.4x, mid 0.7x, fg 1x).
- Magnetic buttons and custom cursor only behind
  `@media (hover: hover) and (pointer: fine)`, movement ≤ 12px.
- Reduced motion: `gsap.matchMedia()` with a calm variant — instant
  opacity, no transforms.

## Typography & texture

- Display serif at fluid scale — `clamp()` up to ~9vw; body 16–18px min,
  60–75ch measure. Maximum 2 families, loaded via next/font or
  self-hosted variable fonts.
- Letter-spacing tightens as size grows (-0.02em at display sizes).
- Texture kills sterility: SVG noise overlay at opacity 0.02–0.04 with
  `mix-blend-mode: overlay`. Frosted glass (`backdrop-filter: blur()`)
  at most once per viewport, with an ultra-thin translucent border.
- Palette: base + ink + ONE accent, all muted. No gradients unless the
  project MASTER.md defines one.

## Performance imperative

A beautiful site that stutters is a failure.
- Composite only: animate `transform` and `opacity`. Never width, height,
  top, or margin.
- `will-change: transform` applied intelligently and removed post-animation.
- Treated images: consistent tone/grain, AVIF/WebP, sized, lazy below fold.
- Accessibility is non-negotiable: 4.5:1 contrast minimum, visible focus
  states styled to the palette, full keyboard paths.

## Implementation ecosystem

- **React / Next.js:** `@gsap/react` (`useGSAP` for scoping/cleanup) +
  `lenis` for smooth scroll under ScrollTrigger. R3F only when MASTER.md
  calls for a single dimensional moment.
- **Astro / vanilla:** GSAP timelines + `lenis` (npm package `lenis` —
  the `@studio-freight/lenis` name is deprecated).

## Do not

- SaaS patterns: three-card feature grids with icons, pill badges, logo
  walls, gradient CTAs.
- Default easings or visible default component styling.
- Emoji as icons; clip-art imagery; marketing filler copy ("Elevate your
  journey") — copy is sparse, declarative, editorial.
- Layout shift from animation. Ever.

